 "verdict": "key partly consistent: 90 signs = 90 letters, 23 groups = 23 words once the plaintext is corrected; one break at the letter level (S3 is غ in غربلت and ع in علتها: same skeleton) and one real break (S6, ل six times, stands for the د of العماد); the last word before اذا دارت (4 signs) is read يظعن on our own reading under a stain, not confirmed",
 "notes": "Rows 11r l.10-13 and 11v l.1-3. By eye 14+15+10+13+14+13+11 = 90 signs (record 14,14,14,15,14,13,13 = 97), 23 dividers (record 24; 11v l.1 opens with one, 11v l.2 and l.3 end with one). Record plaintext corrected from the groups, all checked against the page: (1) غربت is غربلت (5 signs; the page has the ل); (2) المزارت is لمن زارت (groups of 3 and 4: S6 ل, S2 م, S10 ن, then ز ا ر ت); (3) والخلو is والخلق and نقث is نقت, and the next word is وقد: S16 is the same letter in all three, so ق (و/ف would not give وقد); S7 is ت in 8 places, so the last letter of نقت is ت; (4) واحنارت is واختارت (S15 خ as in والخلق); (5) شدو is بدو in the cipher (S5, the ب of غربلت; the page has ش: a cipher/page difference); (6) وهمر is وهم (3 signs; the page's ر is the ز of زوجها); (7) يظهرن is a 4-sign word ending in ن; the page is stained over the middle letters; read يظعن, not confirmed (S23 S24 S25 are singletons); (8) the interlinear 'اذا ادارت' on 11v above l.8 is enciphered text: the chain ends with اذا دارت (S12 S21 S12 | S17 S12 S4 S7), so the verse is two full bayts rhyming in -ارت (زارت, ثارت, اختارت, دارت). Look-alikes kept apart at 3x: S18 (ص-loop with zigzag tail, س in دوسها) vs S22 (ص with round bowl, ج in زوجها); S13 (plain ط, ز in زارت and زوجها) vs S14 (flagged ط, و 6x). ع has three shapes (S8 4x, S3 1x, S25 1x if يظعن is right)."
